    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A palinspastic restoration method has been used to analyze the three-dimensional strain across a North Sea Field. The strains obtained from the restoration have been tested and calibrated using qualitative and quantitative comparison between interpreted values from structure contour maps and computed values of the equivalent theoretical vertical displacement field.\r\n\r\nSeveral tests involving different idealized remote loading states show that using a realistic three-dimensional strain recovered from regional geological data analysis provides the best results. Also, these tests show that idealized remote loading has to be chosen wisely, with careful regards for the tectonic setting.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
